","size":1565901,"stargazers_count":76300,"watchers_count":76300,"language":"Java","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":25807,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":5586,"license":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["elasticsearch","java","search-engine"],"visibility":"public","forks":25807,"open_issues":5586,"watchers":76300,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/pulls/37833","html_url":"https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/37833","diff_url":"https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/37833.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/37833.patch","merged_at":"2019-02-01T08:35:46Z"},"body":"The `terms` aggregator loads the global ordinals to retrieve the cardinality of the field to aggregate on. This information is then used to select the strategy to use for the aggregation (`breadth_first` or `depth_first`). However this should be avoided if the `execution_hint` is explicitly set to `map` since this mode doesn't really need the global ordinals. Since we still need the cardinality of the field this change picks the maximum cardinality in the segments as an estimation of the total cardinality to select the strategy to use (`breadth_first` or `depth_first`). This estimation is only used if the execution hint is set to `map`,  otherwise the global ordinals are still used to retrieve the accurate cardinality.\r\n\r\nCloses #37705","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/37833/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,